      "body": "ACK 4655c2305e80ef19353739a6f66e49442945ed44\r\n\r\nReviewed the code, verified the test locally (on Linux).\r\nChecked that without setting the option the new test fails.\r\nChecked other socket creation places -- other instance found only in `ipc`/`capnp`.\r\nChecked other `SetSockOpt` usages.\r\nLooked into why `TCP_NODELAY` option is set again after accept, while `SO_OOBINLINE` is not. Apparently even setting `TCP_NODELAY` again is extra cautious, and not needed on any of the supported platforms. Inheritance of `SO_OOBINLINE` should be even more reliable, as it is a socket-level option, not TCP level. If the socket option is not inherited, the test would fail. Verified this by unsetting `SO_OOBINLINE` right after the `Accept` in the test (that causes the test to fail).\r\n\r\nI would've liked more adding the test first, then adding the fix and updating the test. It's fine this way too.\r\n",
      "user": {
        "login": "optout21",
        "id": 13562139,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTYyMTM5",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13562139?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/optout21",
